      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I would love to see this addressed. This would allow some better, more immersive controls like moving sliders and dials that are in close proximity to each other. This is very hard to do currently as these items fight for your controllers attention.\n\nIn VR is seems as the distance is calculated based on the boundary of the hand colliders which have a fixed(?) size. Changing this calculation to go from the center of the collider rather than the boundary would allow very fine tuned interactions. This change would not have any meaningful effect that I can think of on existing worlds, as it would only make the interaction distance 1 hand collider radius smaller than it was prior, which is in the bigger picture of things, fairly small. As there cannot currently really exist fine tuned controls (or at worst they are very rare), this change wouldn't really effect anyone but allow for better, immersive controls (among other use cases!)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
